<title>FINLAND: Finland ponders ERM value to credibility - Lipponen.</title>
<headline>Finland ponders ERM value to credibility - Lipponen.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish government must decide this autumn whether linking the markka to Europe's exchange rate mechanism (ERM) would increase economic policy credibility, Prime Minister Paavo Lipponen said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;This autumn we will have to take a stand on whether a link is considered a criterion for EMU and whether it would add credibility to Finland's economic policy,&quot; Lipponen told daily Helsingin Sanomat in an interview.</p>
<p>Lipponen reiterated the government's aim to ensure Finland meets the entry criteria for the third phase of Economic and Monetary Union (EMU).</p>
<p>Lipponen has earlier said Finland will decide for or against ERM in the near future, but has not personally raised the question of ERM membership being a criterion for EMU.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
